{:adr-id "2626000000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-7722 (Renting of video tapes and disks) video-rental-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500" "ADR-2607121200"]
 :mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-5913 (filmdistops.* module shape, Wave 4 human-facing-service class)"

 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 7722 = renting of video tapes and disks -- a video/disk rental
  storefront (checkout/return desk operations, new-release inventory
  restocking, customer service, supplier procurement coordination). Live
  registry.edn :name for \"7722\" independently re-verified fresh via a clean
  clone: exact match \"Renting of video tapes and disks\". No existing repo at
  cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7722 (404) or at the registry's placeholder
  :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-N7722, itself bogus -- wrong org/id-shape,
  also 404). Fresh scaffold, not a repair. Video rental touches two Wave 4
  person-facing-service risk dimensions per ADR-2607152500: age-rating
  admission enforcement and damage/loss consumer-liability decisions --
  closed op allowlist must never include an op that directly finalizes
  either; any 'flag concern' op always escalates, never auto-commit-eligible."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a content-rating admission override (waiving/overriding an age-rating check to admit a rental) -- hard, permanent block"
  "finalizing a damage-liability determination (who owes what for lost/damaged rental inventory) -- hard, permanent block"
  "payment capture/refund, contract negotiation, binding rental-agreement execution -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known fleet-wide bug class: bare-noun scope-excluded-terms (e.g. 'rating',
  'liability') self-match inside the mock advisor's own legitimate default
  rationale text, self-blocking the actor's happy path. Fix: scope-excluded-
  terms phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the age-
  rating admission override', 'finalize the liability determination', JP
  equivalents), never a bare noun -- critical because :flag-customer-
  concern's entire purpose is to discuss age-rating/damage/liability topics
  using exactly those bare nouns. Dedicated regression test
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in
  governor_test.clj asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for a clean
  registered+verified account, never trip :scope-excluded and never
  HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-7722 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/
  Operation/Sim, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5913's filmdistops.* module
  shape module-for-module as vidrentalops.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed accounts directory
    (account-id/name/registered?/verified?, a rental-desk/branch operating
    account), append-only ledger + rental-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-rental-record, schedule-restocking-operation, flag-customer-concern,
    coordinate-supply-order
  - Governor (VidRentalGovernor): 2 named HARD checks (account-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check
    (finalize-content-rating-admission-override / finalize-damage-liability-
    determination / closed 4-op allowlist). always-escalate-ops
    #{:flag-customer-concern}, confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-rental-record only, approval; phase2
    += schedule-restocking-operation/coordinate-supply-order, approval;
    phase3 auto-commits those 3 when clean+confident; flag-customer-concern
    never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval},
    NOT a stub -- mirrors filmdistops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow + all
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory
    self-trip regression), phase_test, governor_contract_test -- 40 tests /
    119 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. README/
    GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT written fresh for this
    domain"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 7722 video-rental-operations-coordination genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "content-rating-admission-override and damage-liability-determination exclusions hardcoded
    in governor checks (scope-exclusion-violations), not just README prose"
   "self-trip bug class fixed by construction (action-phrased terms) + covered
    by dedicated regression test, not avoided by luck"
   "flag-customer-concern always-escalate is a two-layer invariant (governor
    always-escalate-ops + phase's permanent absence from every :auto set)"
   "portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs; clojure -M:lint 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests use
    in-memory MemStore, matching every sibling actor's current maturity"
   "mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor protocol seam
    ready for that swap but not wired in this ADR"]}

